# WHAT RIPGREP SEARCHES THAT GIT IGNORES.
#
# .gitignore hides .se from git, and it is right to: the record, the tokens and
# the scratchpad are this machine's rather than the project's. rg reads
# .gitignore too, so the one folder an agent most often needs to search was the
# one folder it could not.
#
# TWO LINES AND NOT ONE, measured rather than assumed. The first un-ignores the
# folder. The second un-ignores the record inside it, because .gitignore also
# ignores every jsonl file and un-ignoring the folder does not lift that. With
# only the first, rg lists the tokens and never the log.
#
# !.se/** ALONE REACHES NEITHER, because the directory itself stays excluded
# and rg never descends into it.
!.se/
!.se/**/*.jsonl
